---
description: Present a proposal and refine it on reasoned push-back before approval
argument-hint: "[what to propose]"
---
Produce a concrete proposal for: $ARGUMENTS

Present it clearly, then **explicitly invite the user to push back with reasons.**

If they push back:
- Treat their reasons as a mini-interview — ask focused follow-ups only where needed.
- Revise exactly the points they challenged; keep what they accepted.
- Re-present the updated proposal and repeat until they approve.

Do not take irreversible or outward-facing actions until the user has approved.
